card.statement:
Let $\ga$ be a basic classical Lie superalgebra or a queer Lie superalgebra. Then there exists a good $\Z$-grading $\ga =
\oplus_{j \in \Z}\ga_j$ as defined in <<ref:W:Dynkin gr>>. This $\Z$-grading is compatible with the $\Z_2$-grading, that is, $\ga_j =\ga_{j,\bar 0} \oplus \ga_{j,\bar 1}$ where $\ga_{j,a} =
\ga_j \cap \ga_a$ for $a \in \Z_2, j \in \Z$. In particular, we have a refinement of <<ref:W:numbersimple>>:

\begin{equation}
\sudim \ga_e = \sudim \ga_0 + \sudim \ga_1 .
\end{equation}
